<title>CHINA: Earthquake jolts rural region of Tibet.</title>
<headline>Earthquake jolts rural region of Tibet.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring 5.3 on the open-ended Richter scale has jolted China's Himalayan region of Tibet but there were no immediate reports of damage or casualties, Xinhua news agency said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The tremor struck Baxoi county in eastern Tibet at 7.18 p.m. on Friday (1118 GMT), the news agency said.</p>
<p>The epicentre of the earthquake was a rugged, rural region with poor communications, it said.</p>
<p>It gave no more details.</p>
